87	     * exactly the length that country requires. Country codes not listed in
88	     * {@link #NATIONAL_LENGTHS} are accepted on the generic 8-to-15 digit rule alone.
89	     */
90	    /**
91	     * Split E.164 digits (the part after the '+') into {@code { countryCode, nationalNumber }}
92	     * using the recognised country codes (iterated longest/most-specific first, so '+61' wins
93	     * over '+1'). When no known code matches, assumes a two-digit country code — enough to still
94	     * render a '+CC national' display. Used by {@link TelephoneDisplay} to format for humans.
